53632|62356|16|0|1|5|Vertical Bash Chains
53632|62356|16|2|1|5|shard:32
53632|62356|16|4|1|5|0|6|Some enemies allow you to gain $infinite height$ by #bashing them upwards# and #air-stalling# until you can re-bash.\nThe easiest way to do this is by #holding# *Glide* or by *Double Jump*#ing right after bashing#.\n\nKeep in mind that some enemies are easier to work with than others. For example, <purple>Slugs</> are too lightweight and you will fall down before you can regrab it. <purple>Gorleks</> are too heavy and you won't even make them budge.|f=900|instant
3|1|4|17|53632|62356|1|16|0|1|5|Vertical Bash Chains
3|1|4|17|53632|62356|1|16|2|1|5|shard:32
3|1|4|17|53632|62356|1|16|4|1|5|0|6|Some enemies allow you to gain $infinite height$ by #bashing them upwards# and #air-stalling# until you can re-bash.\nThe easiest way to do this is by #holding# *Glide* or by *Double Jump*#ing right after bashing#.\n\nKeep in mind that some enemies are easier to work with than others. For example, <purple>Slugs</> are too lightweight and you will fall down before you can regrab it. <purple>Gorleks</> are too heavy and you won't even make them budge.|f=900|instant
7228|20282|4|17|9|101|1|16|0|1|6|Bash GlideJumps
7228|20282|4|17|9|101|1|16|2|1|6|spell:4002
7228|20282|4|17|9|101|1|16|4|1|6|0|6|*Glide Jumps* are a movement technique that allow you to store $an extra airjump$ as long as you are gliding. The OriRando wiki has an explanation on how they work.\n\nIt just so happens that using *Bash* is also a valid setup for *standing Glide Jumps*. As a rule of thumb: If #both Ori and the enemy# are on solid ground, and #the enemy is slightly above Ori#, you can store a *Glide Jump*.|f=720|instant
3|1|4|17|7228|20282|1|4|17|9|101|1|16|0|1|6|Bash GlideJumps
3|1|4|17|7228|20282|1|4|17|9|101|1|16|2|1|6|spell:4002
3|1|4|17|7228|20282|1|4|17|9|101|1|16|4|1|6|0|6|*Glide Jumps* are a movement technique that allow you to store $an extra airjump$ as long as you are gliding. The OriRando wiki has an explanation on how they work.\n\nIt just so happens that using *Bash* is also a valid setup for *standing Glide Jumps*. As a rule of thumb: If #both Ori and the enemy# are on solid ground, and #the enemy is slightly above Ori#, you can store a *Glide Jump*.|f=720|instant
